= Propositional logic — Technical =

== Syntax ==
Given propositional variables p,q,... and connectives, formulas are generated recursively.

For classical logic:

<pre>
φ ::= p | ¬φ | (φ∧φ) | (φ∨φ) | (φ→φ) | ...
</pre>

== Valuations ==
A valuation:

<pre>
v : Atoms → {0,1}
</pre>

extends recursively to compound formulas according to truth functions.

== Semantic consequence ==
For Γ and φ:

<pre>
Γ ⊨ φ
</pre>

iff every valuation satisfying all formulas in Γ also satisfies φ.

== Decidability ==
Classical propositional validity is decidable.

Truth tables provide an exponential brute-force procedure; SAT algorithms solve large instances using more sophisticated search and learning.

== Complexity ==
Boolean satisfiability is NP-complete, while validity is coNP-complete.

This computational fact concerns decision complexity, not the philosophical meaning of validity.

